<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paramardi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1165–1203</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Paramardideva, Parmal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paramardi was the last powerful king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty">Chandela dynasty</a>, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> from about 1165 to 1203. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a> defeated him and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahoba">Mahoba</a> in 1182, and in 1203 Qutb al-Din Aibak captured his fortress of Kalinjar. His generals Alha and Udal are the heroes of the Alha-Khand ballads.</p></div>
